					5. Table Number Centerpiece Signs: Visibility & Dimensions
				</h2>
				<p>
					Table number signs must balance two opposing goals: they must be large and legible enough for guests to spot from across a crowded, dim reception ballroom, while not being so oversized that they block conversation across the floral centerpiece.
				</p>

				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--accent-blue); margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;">
					5" x 7" vs. 4" x 6" Centerpiece Visibility from 15 Feet Away
				</h3>
				<p>
					Standard <strong>5" x 7" vertical table signs</strong> placed in brass or wooden card stands provide optimal 15–20 foot visibility. For tall floral arrangements on elevated metal stands, ensure the number is positioned between 10" and 14" above the tablecloth so it remains in the clear sightline of standing guests entering the room.
				</p>
